{"slug":"wales-motorcycle-route-map","category":"infographics","title":"Wales: 5 Must-Ride Motorcycle Roads","metaDescription":"Illustrated map of Wales highlighting the 5 best motorcycle roads. Black Mountain Pass, Evo Triangle, Horseshoe Pass and more.","heroImage":"public/images/infographics/wales-motorcycle-route-map.png","author":"VisorUp Team","publishDate":"2026-06-09","readTime":"1 min read","tags":["infographic","shareable","Wales","routes","motorcycle roads"],"relatedSlugs":[],"affiliateLinks":[],"content":"<h2>Wales: 5 Must-Ride Motorcycle Roads</h2><p>Wales packs incredible riding into a compact country. These five roads are essential for any British touring rider.</p><ol><li><strong>Black Mountain Pass</strong> — Brecon Beacons. Wales' finest riding road with dramatic scenery.</li><li><strong>Evo Triangle</strong> — North Wales. Three roads forming a perfect triangle of fast, technical riding near Betws-y-Coed.</li><li><strong>Horseshoe Pass</strong> — North Wales. A sweeping mountain road above Llangollen.</li><li><strong>A470 Snowdonia</strong> — Through the heart of Snowdonia National Park.</li><li><strong>A4069 Black Mountain Road</strong> — South Wales. As featured on Top Gear.</li></ol><p>Total riding: 280+ miles. Best months: April to October. Watch for sheep, single-track roads, and sudden weather changes.</p>"}
